{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED at exact clean pushed head a78c8e0f5692d1e699f95542afc71b99d4bb0d26, artifact 2635d84c at README.md.\\n\\nThe direction is sound: lead with accountable human-agent work and MCP, remove both uncited throughput numbers, keep competitor claims out, and point readers to retained evidence. The exact prose still turns several qualified properties into absolutes.\\n\\nFACTUAL BLOCKERS.\\n1. \"An agent's output is not reproducible from its input\" is absolute and false for outputs that happen to reproduce. The trust argument needs \"need not be reproducible\" or an equally qualified form.\\n2. \"Anyone with a clone can verify the whole history offline\" omits a required boundary. Git does not fetch refs/seq/* in an ordinary clone. The sequence must first be published and attached/fetched; only a clone holding that sequence can verify it offline. First-contact verification also cannot prove that a remote supplied the latest authentic head.\\n3. \"Every actor — a person, or one agent session — signs with its own key\" conflates durable actor identity with an ephemeral process/session. The system explicitly allows several live sessions to use one fingerprint, and resident mode holds actor keys and signs for authenticated session credentials. A signature identifies the actor, not a unique session.\\n4. The list saying \"decisions are durable events\" conflicts with the project model: a decision is the fold's verdict on an act, not a separate durable event. Proposals, ratifications, and review reports are events; decisions are projected on replay.\\n\\nPERFORMANCE. Removing the old ~10 writes/s and ~100k reads/s figures is correct; neither named a workload or machine, and retained performance evidence does not establish the latter. The replacement still overclaims. \"reads to be far faster\" is undefined and has no retained read-throughput evidence. \"Most of that cost is implementation rather than design\" assigns a causal proportion the evidence does not prove. \"identified optimizations have not been taken yet\" ignores the landed append-fixed optimization, although further work remains. \"Both figures\" no longer names two figures. Keep the deliberately vague few-writes wording if desired, state the factual current mechanism and that further optimizations remain, say rates depend on workload and machine, and link the evidence page.\\n\\nARCHITECTURE. This README-only head changes no architecture contract. The signed ordered Git log, Workroom as the first application, MCP as the main agent surface, and gs/browser human surfaces are supported. The actor/session, sequence-fetch, and decision wording above currently misstates those contracts, so approval must wait.\\n\\nSECURITY. No code or authority boundary changes. The current prose nevertheless overpromises attribution and offline audit availability by hiding shared identity/resident custody and refs/seq publication/attachment. Those are security-relevant trust boundaries and must be explicit enough not to imply guarantees the system does not provide.\\n\\nSIMPLIFICATION AND PLAIN ENGLISH. Remove the repeated \"first application\" explanation later in the README or make the later occurrence start directly with the Workroom. Prefer a plainer phrase than \"ground for trust\" if revising that sentence. The opening should describe the record without pitch-like absolutes.\\n\\nVERIFICATION. Exact head, upstream, and actual remote are equal; worktree clean; README-only diff and diff check clean. gofmt, build, vet, and the full uncached 32-package suite passed, including internal/docset. Blog returned HTTP 200; the youtu.be link redirected normally to its YouTube watch page; gitseq.png and docs/reference/performance.md exist. Blog and video links are unchanged. No named competitor appears in the candidate README.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2635d84c799b4380f7a99b5197581daa238cac5b","head":"a78c8e0f5